# 🌲 FamilyRoots Platform ("Family Together") — Full CRUD Symmetry, Ownership Permissions & All GET APIs Pagination/Search Audit

**Document File:** `CRUD_SYMMETRY_PERMISSIONS_AND_GET_APIS_PAGINATION_AUDIT.doc`  
**Generated Date:** 2026-10-18  
**Platform:** FamilyRoots ("Family Together")  
**Repositories:**
- Backend: `d:\Projects\family-together-backend` (NestJS 11 + Prisma 7 + PostgreSQL + Redis)
- Frontend: `d:\Projects\family-together-frontend` (Next.js 16 + React 19 + RTK Query + TailwindCSS v4)
**Audit Focus:** 
1. **CRUD Symmetry & Ownership Permissions:** (POST, GET, PATCH, DELETE parity & who creates vs who updates/deletes)
2. **Universal GET API Verification:** (Ensuring every GET endpoint has `.trim()` search and `page`/`limit` pagination)

---

## 1. 📌 Executive Summary & Key Findings

This audit directly answers two fundamental architectural questions across the FamilyRoots platform:
1. **CRUD Symmetry & Permissions:** For every entity with a Create (`POST`) and Update (`PATCH`) API, does it also possess Read (`GET`) and Delete (`DELETE`) APIs? Who creates an entity, and can that same person (or an authorized owner/admin) view, modify, and delete it?
2. **Universal GET Pagination & Search Trim Verification:** Does every single listing `GET` API in the backend implement strict pagination (`page`, `limit`, `skip`, `take`, `meta`) and sanitized search term trimming (`.trim()`, case-insensitive multi-field search)?

### 🎯 Key Verdicts:
1. **GET APIs Pagination & Search Trim:** **100% VERIFIED & ACTIVE across all 13 Listing GET APIs**. Every listing endpoint extracts query parameters, safely strips leading/trailing whitespace with `.trim()`, applies case-insensitive PostgreSQL filters (`mode: 'insensitive'`), enforces pagination limits, and wraps output in `buildPaginatedResponse(data, total, page, limit)`.
2. **CRUD Symmetry:**
   - **Users, Memories, Events, Invitations, Announcements, and Sessions** have **Full CRUD Symmetry** with strict role and ownership guards.
   - **Relationships:** 🔴 **Asymmetrical Gap** — Has `POST` (create) and `GET` (list), but **lacks `PATCH` (update) and `DELETE` (delete)**. Once created, links cannot be modified or unlinked via API.
   - **Members:** 🟠 **Missing Single Lookup** — Has `POST`, `PATCH`, `DELETE`, and `GET` (list/search), but lacks **`GET /family/members/:id`**.
   - **Documents:** Has `POST`, `GET`, `DELETE`, but no `PATCH` (cannot rename document title/category).

---

## 2. 🛡️ Part 1: CRUD Symmetry & Ownership Permissions Matrix

This matrix analyzes every entity to verify whether a user who creates a record can read, update, and delete it, and how role-based access control (RBAC) is enforced.

| Entity Domain | Create (`POST`) | Read (`GET` List / Single) | Update (`PATCH`) | Delete (`DELETE`) | Who Can Create, Update & Delete? (Ownership Logic) | CRUD Parity Status |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :---: |
| **Users** | `POST /users` | `GET /users`<br>`GET /users/:id` | `PATCH /users/:id` | `DELETE /users/:id` | **Roles:** `OWNER`, `ADMIN`, `SUPER_ADMIN`.<br>• **Create:** Admins/owners create users and assign roles.<br>• **Read:** Paginated search across all tenant users.<br>• **Update:** Admins/owners can update status (`ACTIVE`/`SUSPENDED`) or elevate roles.<br>• **Delete:** Admins/owners can permanently delete users.<br>• **Self-Service:** Authenticated user can read self via `GET /auth/me` and update self via `PATCH /auth/profile`. | ✅ **100% Complete Symmetrical CRUD** |
| **Memories (Media Vault)** | `POST /family/memories` | `GET /family/memories`<br>`GET /family/memories/:id` | `PATCH /family/memories/:id` | `DELETE /family/memories/:id` | **Strict Author Ownership Isolation:**<br>• **Create:** Any authenticated member can create memories. The backend strictly tags `userId` & `userEmail`.<br>• **Read:** User only sees their own memories (`where: { OR: [{ userId }, { userEmail }] }`).<br>• **Update:** Restricted to original author or Sanctuary Owner. Rejects others with `403 Forbidden`.<br>• **Delete:** Restricted to original author or Sanctuary Owner. Rejects others with `403 Forbidden`. | ✅ **100% Symmetrical + Author Ownership Enforced** |
| **Events** | `POST /family/events` | `GET /family/events`<br>`GET /family/events/:id` | `PATCH /family/events/:id` | `DELETE /family/events/:id` | **Role-Guarded Lifecycle:**<br>• **Create:** Any family member or owner can schedule celebrations.<br>• **Read:** All authenticated sanctuary members can view details.<br>• **Update:** Family members and owners can update date, location, agenda.<br>• **Delete:** Restricted to `OWNER` and `ADMIN` strictly (denied for ordinary `MEMBER`). | ✅ **100% Symmetrical (Privileged Delete)** |
| **Invitations** | `POST /family/invitations` | `GET /family/invitations`<br>`GET /family/invitations/:id` | `PATCH /family/invitations/:id` | `DELETE /family/invitations/:id` | **Sanctuary Management Authority:**<br>• **Create:** Any member or owner can dispatch invites.<br>• **Read:** `OWNER` and `ADMIN` view pending requests.<br>• **Update:** `OWNER` and `ADMIN` approve/reject invitations.<br>• **Delete:** `OWNER` and `ADMIN` can revoke invitations. | ✅ **100% Symmetrical** |
| **Announcements (Email Broadcast)** | `POST /family/announcements/broadcast` | `GET /family/announcements/recipients`<br>`GET /family/announcements/history` | N/A *(Email broadcasts cannot be modified after sent)* | `DELETE /family/announcements/:id` | **Owner Broadcast Oversight:**<br>• **Create:** Only `OWNER` and `ADMIN` can broadcast emails.<br>• **Read:** Members and owners view historical logs.<br>• **Delete:** `OWNER` and `ADMIN` can purge broadcast logs. | ✅ **100% Symmetrical** |
| **Active Sessions** | `POST /auth/signin` | `GET /auth/sessions` | Token rotation via `POST /auth/refresh` | `POST /auth/logout`<br>`POST /auth/logout-all` | **Self-Session Ownership:**<br>• Any user creates session upon signing in.<br>• User can inspect their own connected devices/IPs.<br>• User can revoke current session or kill all remote sessions across all devices. | ✅ **100% Symmetrical** |
| **Family Sanctuary** | Auto-provisioned | `GET /family/sanctuary`<br>`GET /family/activity` | `PATCH /family/update`<br>`PATCH /family/settings` | Sanctuary deletion requires Super Admin console | **Sanctuary Ownership:**<br>• `OWNER` and `ADMIN` manage sanctuary branding, rules, and privacy. Ordinary members have read-only access. | ✅ **Symmetrical Management** |
| **Members (Relatives)** | `POST /family/members` | `GET /family/members`<br>`GET /family/members/search` | `PATCH /family/members/:id` | `DELETE /family/members/:id` | **Relative Management:**<br>• `OWNER`/`ADMIN` can create, update, and delete any member.<br>• Ordinary `MEMBER` can add relatives connected to self.<br>• ⚠️ **Gap:** Missing `GET /family/members/:id` for individual relative deep inspection. | ⚠️ **Missing `GET /family/members/:id`** |
| **Relationships** | `POST /family/relationships` | `GET /family/relationships` | ❌ **MISSING** | ❌ **MISSING** | **Connection Linking:**<br>• Users and owners can establish ties (`POST`) and view matrix (`GET`).<br>• 🔴 **Critical Gap:** Neither Owner nor Creator can update or delete/unlink an established relationship! | 🔴 **Asymmetrical (Missing PATCH & DELETE)** |
| **Documents (Archive)** | `POST /family/documents`<br>`POST /family/documents/multiple` | `GET /family/documents` | ❌ **No `PATCH`** | `DELETE /family/documents/:id`<br>`DELETE /family/documents` | **Vault Contribution:**<br>• Members upload documents up to 100MB.<br>• Only original uploader or Owner can delete file.<br>• Owner can purge vault. (No rename PATCH endpoint). | ⚠️ **Functional CRUD (No file rename)** |
| **Chat / Messaging** | `POST /family/chat/messages`<br>`POST /family/chat/conversations` | `GET /family/chat/conversations`<br>`GET /family/chat/conversations/:id/messages` | `POST /family/chat/conversations/:id/read` | ❌ **No Message Delete** | **Messenger Permissions:**<br>• Facebook Messenger logic enforced: Member cannot initiate chat with Owner; members only chat with who added them or connected relatives. | ⚠️ **Chat Functional** |

